            William James (1842–1910), the Harvard physician, psychologist,
            and philosopher whose work helped shape modern psychology and
            American pragmatism, left behind an unusually revealing documentary
            record of his encounters with homeopathy—one that stretches from
            his medical training into the final years of his life.
          </p>
