            William James to Henry James Jr., November 24, 1872.
            <em> The Correspondence of William James</em>,
            edited by Ignas K. Skrupskelis and Elizabeth M. Berkeley,
            vol. 1, p. 178.
          </p>

          <p>
            Croce reproduces the passage in
            <em> Young William James Thinking</em>, p. 112.
            His accompanying note 48 identifies the letter’s date,
            recipient, volume, and page.
          </p>

          <p class="source-note">
            I follow the quotation and reference supplied by Croce;
            I have not examined the original manuscript myself.
            This passage documents James’s personal report of benefit.
          </p>

